    "note_tweet": {
      "entities": {},
      "text": "China has only recently begun its visa-free transit policy, and previously, obtaining a Chinese visa was not much more difficult than obtaining a US visa. Seek common ground while reserving differences, I will solve your worries🤗\n\nDownload Nihao China. It is official App by UnionPay, including Baidu maps, some services. However, I still recommend you download Amap (Gaode Maps), because while Google Maps can tell you where you are, it can't provide accurate route planning. iPhones automatically switch to Amap in China, so there's no need to download Amap.\n\nDownload Alipay or WeChat, Alipay fully supports linking foreign cards, but WeChat Pay is more widely used by small vendors.\nDidi already has mini-programs on Alipay and WeChat, so there's no need to download the app. Unless you need to directly link your bank card, Mastercard Rewards usually offers cashback programs, but you'll need to register in advance.\n\nDownload redteaGO to get eSIM. Using \"SUJI0003\" get 3USD, supports three major carriers, no VPN required, and no need to worry about losing connection.\n\nSo far, you've solved your payment issues in China. To use a card directly, you'll need to find merchants with UMS (UnionPay Merchant Services) POS machines, such as chain restaurants like Haidilao Hot Pot and Starbucks."
    },
